      "decision": "Potential mgh uses chosen zero level, not absolute disappearance of all energy at floor. SourcePDF147 prose says potential change equals work despite formulaA=-deltaEp, and confuses lifting work sign; teach gravitational work Ep1-Ep2, lifting agent opposite sign for uniform raise. Numeric h>=0 branch explicit, not universal nonnegative potential. g9.8/10 supplied, old6g9.81N/kg preserved."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        148,
        149,
        150
      ],
      "decision": "Kinetic energy uses speed magnitude, positive mass; net work deltaEk not motor work alone when drag present. Negative net braking work, not negative Ek. Direction reversal alone with same speed gives sameEk, distinct from momentum. Exact square/gram/unit oracles."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        150,
        151,
        152,
        153,
        154,
        155
      ],
      "decision": "Source closed system mechanical energy always constant overstates law; conservation requires no dissipative conversion/unaccounted external work. Text itself discusses heatingPDF154; original lesson makes condition explicit, total energy conserved. Gravity reference level and before-impact cutoff. Spring kx²/2 limited linear elastic regime. Negative inferred Ek2 is impossible model state, validator rejects. No assumed equality maximumEk=maximumEp without initial/rest/zero-level conditions."
    },
